  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Ha. Like 'h' in 'hello' or 'home'. A soft breath of air the softest H sound in Arabic!",
      "title": "Meet Ha!",
      "ar": "ه",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Ha"
    },
    {
      "en": "Changes shape dramatically in different positions practice all four forms carefully! Ha is a soft BREATH imagine breathing out gently on a cold day. Light and airy!",
      "title": "How to write Ha"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Ha says “ha”.",
      "title": "Ha with fatha",
      "ar": "هَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Ha says “he”.",
      "title": "Ha with kasra",
      "ar": "هِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Ha says “ho”.",
      "title": "Ha with damma",
      "ar": "هُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“Guidance is from Allah”",
